      "text": "The pope should have the power to depose a ruler and release that ruler's subjects from their allegiance.",
      "value": 2,
      "rationale": "Dictatus papae claims that the pope may depose emperors and release subjects from fealty to wicked rulers, and the deposing power was later exercised against Henry IV.",
