      "text": "The highest religious authority should be able to judge the rulers of states, and no earthly authority may judge it in return.",
      "value": 2,
      "rationale": "Unam sanctam says the spiritual power judges the temporal while the highest power can be judged by God alone, and Dictatus papae says no one may judge the pope.",
      "sources": [
        "s1",
        "s2"
      ],
      "addedAs": "clerical-rule"
    },
    {
      "text": "Religious authority holds the superior right over all property, and laypeople hold it only by use and on condition of just conduct.",
      "value": 1,
      "rationale": "Giles of Rome argued the church has direct dominion over all property and can recover goods misused, a distinctive hierocratic claim no statement captures.",
      "sources": [
